WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.559
Nicole: So, what do you do
if your system gets infected?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.090
The first step in incident response
if you are concerned that a device or

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:10.980
system may be infected is containment.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.349
It’s important to disconnect from the
internet and the network you’re on as this

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:19.860
will prevent any more data being sent to
a malware server or will stop it spreading

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.640
to other computers on your network.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.630
Stay offline as much as possible unless
needing to download any legitimate

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.599
tools to help get rid of the malware.

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:32.820
Disconnect after the download
is complete and stay offline

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:34.689
until the malware is removed.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.780
Opening a system in safe mode or
safe boot allows only the minimum

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.700
software and programs to load.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.370
Logging in to accounts should be
avoided whilst removing malware so

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:50.930
as not to expose passwords through
copy and paste function or by 'show

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:55.510
password' because 'key logger' malware
is a common component of malware.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:01.650
Also avoid sharing any personal details or
information whilst a device is infected.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.450
Check activity monitors for malicious
applications especially if a suspicious

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.889
update or application has been installed.

00:01:10.699 --> 00:01:12.149
Run a malware scanner.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.600
These can remove most standard infections
however if your antivirus software hasn't

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.609
already picked this up you should try
another scanner which may be able to

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:27.350
detect more existing and emerging malware
such as a heuristic antimalware solution.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.770
Verify the browser homepage this will
involve connecting to the internet and

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:37.610
clear the cache, this is the temporary
storage location where data is saved.

00:01:38.309 --> 00:01:42.689
If malware removal is unsuccessful,
it may be that the operating system

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:47.279
may need to be reinstalled along with
applications and programs from scratch.

00:01:47.879 --> 00:01:51.890
If everything is backed up it shouldn't
be a problem but contacting the system

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.220
suppliers help desk may be necessary.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:00.270
This process is exactly the same for large
companies and organisations but is usually

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.910
handled by tools that do these steps
or a dedicated incident response team.

